          + 9. to set out, to start to go: umalis
          + 10. to spread out to show, sell, or use: magkalat, ikalat
          + 11. to set to, to begin: magsimula, simulan, mag-umpisa,
            umpisahan

   understood
   adj.
     *
          + known: alam, nalalaman, batid, nababatid, talastas,
            natatalastas

   out
   adj.
     *
          + 1. not at home, away from office, work, etc.: wala (sa bahay,
            opisina, atb.), nasa labas
          + 2. not burning, not lighted: patay
          + 3. not correct: mali, sala
          + 4. made known, e.g. a secret: hayag na, alam na
          + 5. into the open so as to be seen: litaw adv. 1. forth:
            palabas, papalabas
          + 2. aloud, plainly: malakas, maliwanag
          + 3. out of, not within: wala, nasa labas
          + 4. beyond the reach of: napakalayo, di maabot
          + 5. without: wala
          + 6. because of: dahil sa
          + 7. from: sa, mula sa

   know
   v.
     *
          + 1. to know: alam
          + 2. to know someone: makilala, kilalanin
          + 3. to have knowledge of: malaman, mabatid
          + 4. to understand: umunawa, maunawaan
          + 5. to learn: matuto, matutuhan
          + 6. to let know: ipaalam, ipabatid, sabihin, pagsabihan,
            ibalita, balitaan

   adj.
     *
          + to be thoroughly familiar with: marunong, maalam

   aywan
   phrase.
     *
          + be ignorant of something. Aywan ko. I don't know. [var. ewan]
            [syn. di alam]

   ha
   int.
     *
          + interrogative meaning: What is it?, What do you mean?, What's
            that again? [syn. ano?, ano kamo?] part. interrogative
            particle meaning: Do you understand? [syn. Alam mo na ba, ha?]
            part. exclamatory interrogative particle with the element of
            surprise or reproach: Is that so? [syn. Ganoon pala, ha? So
            that's what it is, huh?]
          + 2.) ha! intj. (deprecatingly) So!, (reproachingly) So, that's
            it!, particle producing laughter (in series) Ha! Ha! Ha!

   paalam
   intj.
     *
          + farewell (from alam)

   v.
     *
          + magpaalam (mag-) to bid goodbye. Magpaalam ka sa iyong ina.
            Say goodbye to your mother.


